5. The most important coding patterns from today
Pattern 1: Safe collection access


java
if (list == null || list.isEmpty()) {
    continue;
}
Always check for null before calling list methods.

Pattern 2: Aggregate and count


java
total += value;
count++;
Useful for averages, totals, statistics, and grouped reporting.

Pattern 3: Filter using multiple conditions


java
if (conditionA && conditionB) {
    result.add(item);
}
Translate each business requirement into an explicit condition.

Pattern 4: Initialize accumulators at the correct scope


java
for (Member member : members) {
    double total = 0.0;
    // Process this member's workouts
}
Initialize once per member, not once per workout. Otherwise, your totals reset unexpectedly.

Pattern 5: Add instead of overwrite


java
total += charge;
Use += when accumulating a running total; use = when intentionally replacing a value.

